Ludwig van Beethoven's Sixth Symphony is  known as the pastoral and now this  masterpiece is at the center of an  ambitious global project the composer  intended it as an homage to rural life  and nature  the person with the postural Beethoven  composed the word that was particularly  about the relationship between man and  nature with an eye towards this piece of  music we want to focus attention on our  own relationship with nature which of  course today is conditioned by  Environmental Protection and climate  change  the Beethoven pastoral project connects  the Masters music with 21st century  environmental conservation it was  unveiled at the UN climate change  conference Cup 23 in Beethoven's  birthplace Bonn Germany in principle the  pastoral project addresses musicians in  all genres a publicity clip presents  various musicians as project ambassadors  I mean I always like the stories about  Beethoven he would be seen walking in  nature communing with his music but also  with the birds and ourselves what you  hear the idea of transferring the  postural to another world stylistically  interested me right away as did the  project connected with it  I found combining the pastoral nature  and the climate conference very  intriguing  [Music]  jazz violinist Gregor Huebner was one of  the musicians on hand in buns Beethoven  house he presented some of his own  improvisations on the pastoral  a pasta Valley is really the pastoral is  difficult because Beethoven is so good  at developing motifs he can spin a  single motif into a whole symphony the  project ambassadors in this promotional  clip show how it's done  whether rehearsal or performance and  regardless of the instrument what counts  is the final product a unique  interpretation of Beethoven's Pastoral  Symphony  [Music]  the apostolate talk Austral day will be  the high point and the culmination of  the project it will come inside with the  UN World Environment Day on June the 5th  2020 and it will feature as many  variations on the pastoral as possible  played across the globe there are still  two and a half years to go until that  date in the meantime we want to  establish a pastoral network connecting  artists all over the world part of the  Beethoven pastoral project and the BT HV  and 2020 stand up for the preservation  of nature with your pastoral music  starting on June 5th 2018 the next World  Environment Day musicians from all over  the world can present their ideas on the  Internet of how to combine Beethoven's  timeless music with a modern love of  nature  [Music]  you
 

